# Project specific
# Feature worktrees live in-repo at .worktrees/ and are full checkouts
# (~1.1 GB each). CI builds from a fresh clone so they never exist there,
# but a local `docker build .` would otherwise ship every one of them as
# build context.
.worktrees/
pocketbase/pb_data/
pocketbase/backups/
pocketbase/*.log
pocketbase/*.db
pocketbase/pocketbase
drive/
backups/
outputs/
logs/
*.log
*.db
*.sqlite
csv_history/

# Private config that no image reads (kindred#2575)
#
# kindred#2575 narrowed each Dockerfile to copy config/ BY NAME, so none of
# these reaches an image today. They are excluded from the build CONTEXT as
# well because that is the layer that does not depend on getting a COPY glob
# right: a future `config/branding.prod.json` would be picked up by
# Dockerfile.api's `config/branding*.json` without anyone noticing, and the
# three files below are the ones where that would actually matter.
#
# google_sheets.json is the Google SERVICE-ACCOUNT KEY. It is gitignored and
# absent from CI, but it is a real file in a dev checkout, which is the whole
# reason it is named first.
config/google_sheets.json
# Read by the Go binary from the /config volume at runtime, never from an
# image -- Dockerfile.pocketbase copies no config at all.
config/lodging_registry.json
# No code reader anywhere in the repo; only the symlink setup scripts.
config/sheets_sharing.local.json

